#    tools/aie_timing_slice.py, whose latencies are SPEC(Peano) from llvm-aie AIE2Schedule.td (snapshot a36c62b9),
#    not measured. The overlay binary and its disassembly stay in git-ignored scratch; only addresses and
#    mnemonics are quoted here.
#
# Pre-registration A (sha256 915ccda7c9f616b7a9709b4bd07beb073f13f9d578812ccac18c64959e024abf):
#   written_utc 2026-10-12T20:37:01Z, before any mode-4 point has run.
#   question: does the fused load+upshift vlda.ups.s32.s8 (the DPU overlay's form, pm_0002 0x24d4) decode its runtime shift scalar like register vups (mode 3: k = s & 63, saturating left)?
#   why: a timing-aware slice of pm_0002 (scratch tslice.py, llvm-aie AIE2Schedule.td a36c62b9: lda def 7, vlda.ups shift read at 7) gives s3 = the sign-extended byte at param-struct +0x20 with nothing else writing s3 in 0x2200..0x2600. Mode 3 says vups(5) shifts by 5, the DPU shifts by 1. Either vlda.ups decodes differently, or struct+0x20 is not the raw REG_0 0x7B byte.
#   test: srs_probe.py --modes 4 --shifts=-128:255; same 32 int8 lanes as mode 3, loaded from memory. The kernel object is disassembled afterwards to confirm the compiler emitted vlda.ups (if not, the run tests nothing new and is reported as such).
#   decision rule: H_same holds iff every scalar's fit equals mode 3's (k = s & 63 saturating). Any scalar that differs refutes it, and the per-scalar map is recorded.
#
# Pre-registration B, the struct check (sha256 0b3aa113c6723d3e4ea6b46df09a3c52fd6d37d3947ff9349fb5b75869c140f4):
#   written_utc 2026-10-12T20:40:57Z, before any REG_0 byte at a resolved struct offset has been read.
#   question: is the param struct at [p3] in pm_0002 0x21f8..0x228a a verbatim copy of REG_0, with struct+0x21 = REG_0 0x7C (so p3 = REG_0 + 0x5B)?
#   method: resolve every [p3, djN] / [p3, #imm] offset in that stretch from the nearest preceding dj write (timing-aware), read REG_0[0x5B + off] with the load's width from the fixture xmodel, and compare with the fixture conv's parameters.
#   prediction: NOT verbatim (the values will not read as the fixture's parameters), because the adjacent byte 0x21 passes raw into vsrs while 0x20 cannot pass raw into vlda.ups. Weak: a static read, no execution trace.

